     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, about 91 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is twice the maximum daily dose and in the range where serious toxicity is expected, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. I don't know of any indication that calls for it, and a higher dose won't give more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. The harm would likely fall on the patient, so I can't enter it on a chart note alone.\n\nThis isn't a judgment on your authority. If you think there's a rationale I'm missing, you can enter the order yourself and it will go through pharmacy verification. A second review is a sensible step for a dose like this.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the aim is stronger pain control or anti-inflammatory effect, I can also help with a multimodal regimen. Just tell me which option you want."
      }
